IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc-core-bodies`
IMPORT `uc3-periods`
IMPORT `uc3-disability-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch1-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-bedrooms`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 1 paragraph 1, Schedule 4 paragraphs 1 to 2, 4, 9 to 12 and 26 to 29: tests of layer 1.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text).
--
-- EVERY EXPECTED VALUE IS WRITTEN HERE FROM THE TEXT, beside the assertion, before the file was run: none was copied from what the encoding printed.
-- Where an expected value rests on a reading the text does not settle, the comment names the fork (U3-F8 month counting, U3-F9 sex groups,
-- U3-F11 disabled child) in NOTES.md. A helper below is named "uc3 test" because every name sits in one folder after the merge.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers: records built from a few knobs, because L4 has no record update.

-- Payment number n (1 care component of disability living allowance, 2 care component of child disability payment, 3 care component of Scottish
-- adult disability living allowance, 4 attendance allowance, 5 pension age disability payment, 6 daily living component of personal independence
-- payment, 7 daily living component of adult disability payment) has the status given; the other six are neither received nor so entitled.
GIVEN i IS A NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
      status IS A `Status of a disability payment`
GIVETH A `Status of a disability payment`
`uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` i n status MEANS
    IF i EQUALS n THEN status ELSE `neither received nor so entitled`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      status IS A `Status of a disability payment`
GIVETH A `Disability payments of a person`
`uc3 test — only payment n has the status` n status MEANS
    `Disability payments of a person` WITH
        `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 1 n status
        `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 2 n status
        `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 3 n status
        `attendance allowance` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 4 n status
        `pension age disability payment` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 5 n status
        `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 6 n status
        `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 7 n status

GIVETH A `Disability payments of a person`
`uc3 test — no disability payment` MEANS
    `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` 0 `received by the person`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Disability payments of a person`
`uc3 test — only payment n is received` n MEANS
    `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` n `received by the person`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Disability payments of a person`
`uc3 test — only payment n is entitled to but not received` n MEANS
    `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` n `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The lists of payments. Seven places in the text list disability payments, and the lists differ. Each is tested payment by payment.

-- Sch 3 para 5(3)(b), Sch 4 para 12(3)(a), 12(6A)(a), 15(2)(b) to (da): seven payments, all "in receipt of".
-- Expected: every one of the seven received gives TRUE; none received gives FALSE; entitled to but not received gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 2)
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 3)
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 4)
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 5)
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6)
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` `uc3 test — no disability payment`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is entitled to but not received` 1))

-- Sch 4 para 12(6)(a): the disabled child condition names only two payments, the care component of disability living allowance (i) and of child disability payment (ii).
-- Expected: payments 1 and 2 give TRUE; each of 3 to 7 gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) — a child in receipt of one of the listed care components` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) — a child in receipt of one of the listed care components` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) — a child in receipt of one of the listed care components` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 3))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) — a child in receipt of one of the listed care components` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 4))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) — a child in receipt of one of the listed care components` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 5))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) — a child in receipt of one of the listed care components` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) — a child in receipt of one of the listed care components` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7))

-- Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea): six payments, and the care component of child disability payment is not among them (16(2)(c) is disability living allowance,
-- (ca) Scottish adult disability living allowance, (d) attendance allowance, (da) pension age disability payment, (e) personal independence payment, (ea) adult disability payment).
-- Expected: payments 1, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 give TRUE; payment 2 gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 2))
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 3)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 4)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 5)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7)

-- Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) (and 16(2)(f)): "entitled to a payment within paragraph (b), (bb), (c), (ca), (d) or (da) but is not receiving it": the same six payments, without the child one.
-- Expected: entitled but not receiving payments 1, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 gives TRUE; payment 2 gives FALSE; receiving a payment gives FALSE (that is limb (b) and the others).
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` (`uc3 test — only payment n is entitled to but not received` 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` (`uc3 test — only payment n is entitled to but not received` 2))
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` (`uc3 test — only payment n is entitled to but not received` 3)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` (`uc3 test — only payment n is entitled to but not received` 4)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` (`uc3 test — only payment n is entitled to but not received` 5)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` (`uc3 test — only payment n is entitled to but not received` 6)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` (`uc3 test — only payment n is entitled to but not received` 7)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 1))

-- Sch 4 para 29(5): "under 35 and in receipt of" six payments: (a) disability living allowance, (aa) child disability payment, (ab) Scottish adult disability living allowance,
-- (b) attendance allowance, (c) personal independence payment, (d) adult disability payment. Pension age disability payment is not among them.
-- Expected: payments 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 and 7 give TRUE; payment 5 gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(5) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(5) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 2)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(5) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 3)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(5) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 4 para 29(5) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 5))
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(5) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6)
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(5) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Schedule 1 paragraph 1: the definitions that Schedule 4 paragraph 29(10) borrows.

GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      s275 IS A BOOLEAN
      healthService IS A BOOLEAN
      wales IS A BOOLEAN
      scotland IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Hospital that may be an independent hospital`
`uc3 test — a hospital` nation s275 healthService wales scotland MEANS
    `Hospital that may be an independent hospital` WITH
        `a hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS s275
        `a health service hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS healthService
        `an independent hospital as the meaning is assigned to it by section 2 of the Care Standards Act 2000` IS wales
        `an independent health care service as defined in section 10F(1)(a) and (b) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978` IS scotland

-- "independent hospital": (a) England, a hospital under section 275 that is not a health service hospital under it; (b) Wales, section 2 of the Care Standards Act 2000;
-- (c) Scotland, an independent health care service under section 10F(1)(a) and (b).
-- Expected: England with a hospital that is not a health service hospital gives TRUE; England with a health service hospital gives FALSE; England with no hospital gives FALSE;
-- Wales reads only the Wales fact (an England-only hospital gives FALSE there, and a Wales fact gives TRUE); Scotland reads only the Scotland fact.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — independent hospital` England (`uc3 test — a hospital` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — independent hospital` England (`uc3 test — a hospital` England TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — independent hospital` England (`uc3 test — a hospital` England FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — independent hospital` Wales (`uc3 test — a hospital` Wales TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — independent hospital` Wales (`uc3 test — a hospital` Wales FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — independent hospital` Scotland (`uc3 test — a hospital` Scotland TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — independent hospital` Scotland (`uc3 test — a hospital` Scotland FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE

GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      england IS A BOOLEAN
      wales IS A BOOLEAN
      scotland IS A BOOLEAN
      hospital IS A `Hospital that may be an independent hospital`
GIVETH A `Premises that may be a care home`
`uc3 test — premises` nation england wales scotland hospital MEANS
    `Premises that may be a care home` WITH
        `nation of Great Britain in which the premises are` IS nation
        `a care home within the meaning of section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000` IS england
        `a place at which a care home service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016 is provided wholly or mainly to persons aged 18 or over` IS wales
        `a care home service within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010` IS scotland
        `the premises as a hospital that may be an independent hospital` IS hospital

-- "care home": (a) England, section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000; (aa) Wales, a place providing a care home service under Part 1 of the 2016 Act wholly or
-- mainly to persons aged 18 or over; (b) Scotland, a care home service under paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the 2010 Act; (c) in any of the above cases, includes an independent hospital.
-- Expected: each nation reads only its own fact; an England fact on Welsh premises gives FALSE; an independent hospital is a care home in any nation.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — care home` (`uc3 test — premises` England TRUE FALSE FALSE (`uc3 test — a hospital` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — care home` (`uc3 test — premises` Wales TRUE FALSE FALSE (`uc3 test — a hospital` Wales FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — care home` (`uc3 test — premises` Wales FALSE TRUE FALSE (`uc3 test — a hospital` Wales FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — care home` (`uc3 test — premises` Scotland FALSE TRUE FALSE (`uc3 test — a hospital` Scotland FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — care home` (`uc3 test — premises` Scotland FALSE FALSE TRUE (`uc3 test — a hospital` Scotland FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — care home` (`uc3 test — premises` England FALSE FALSE FALSE (`uc3 test — a hospital` England TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — care home` (`uc3 test — premises` Scotland FALSE FALSE FALSE (`uc3 test — a hospital` Scotland FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — care home` (`uc3 test — premises` England FALSE FALSE FALSE (`uc3 test — a hospital` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS FALSE

-- "registered charity": a charity entered in the register under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011, or a body entered on the Scottish register.
-- Expected: either limb alone gives TRUE; neither gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — registered charity` (`Charity that may be a registered charity` WITH `entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011` IS TRUE, `entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` IS FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — registered charity` (`Charity that may be a registered charity` WITH `entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE, `entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — registered charity` (`Charity that may be a registered charity` WITH `entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE, `entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

GIVEN moveable IS A BOOLEAN
      sleeping IS A BOOLEAN
      caravan IS A BOOLEAN
      mobile IS A BOOLEAN
      houseboat IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Structure that may be a tent`
`uc3 test — a structure` moveable sleeping caravan mobile houseboat MEANS
    `Structure that may be a tent` WITH
        `moveable structure` IS moveable
        `designed or adapted (solely or mainly) for the purpose of sleeping in a place for any period` IS sleeping
        `caravan` IS caravan
        `mobile home` IS mobile
        `houseboat` IS houseboat

-- "tent": a moveable structure designed or adapted (solely or mainly) for sleeping in a place for any period, that is not a caravan, a mobile home or a houseboat.
-- Expected: moveable and for sleeping and none of the three gives TRUE; failing the first or second gives FALSE; each of the three gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — tent` (`uc3 test — a structure` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — tent` (`uc3 test — a structure` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — tent` (`uc3 test — a structure` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — tent` (`uc3 test — a structure` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — tent` (`uc3 test — a structure` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — tent` (`uc3 test — a structure` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of council`
      publicAuthority IS A BOOLEAN
      nonProfit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Body that may be a voluntary organisation`
`uc3 test — a body` kind publicAuthority nonProfit MEANS
    `Body that may be a voluntary organisation` WITH
        `public authority` IS publicAuthority
        `the body as a possible local authority` IS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
            `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS England
            `kind of body` IS kind
        `activities are carried on otherwise than for profit` IS nonProfit

-- "voluntary organisation": a body (other than a public or local authority) whose activities are carried on otherwise than for profit.
-- Expected: a body that is neither and is not for profit gives TRUE; a public authority gives FALSE; an English county council (a local authority in England under regulation 2) gives FALSE;
-- a body run for profit gives FALSE; an English parish council is a local authority too (regulation 2 lists it for England) and gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — voluntary organisation` (`uc3 test — a body` `another kind of body` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — voluntary organisation` (`uc3 test — a body` `another kind of body` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — voluntary organisation` (`uc3 test — a body` `a county council` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — voluntary organisation` (`uc3 test — a body` `another kind of body` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1 — voluntary organisation` (`uc3 test — a body` `a parish council` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Schedule 4 paragraph 1(2): a renter, and a joint renter.
-- Reg 26(2) is taken as a fact (uc1). Expected: a claimant to whom reg 26(2) applies is a renter; a joint renter is a renter whose claim is a joint claim.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 1(2) — a claimant is a renter` (`Claimant who may be a renter` WITH `regulation 26(2) applies to the claimant` IS TRUE, `claim basis` IS `a single claimant`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 1(2) — a claimant is a renter` (`Claimant who may be a renter` WITH `regulation 26(2) applies to the claimant` IS FALSE, `claim basis` IS `a single claimant`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 1(2) — a joint renter` (`Claimant who may be a renter` WITH `regulation 26(2) applies to the claimant` IS TRUE, `claim basis` IS `joint claimants`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 1(2) — a joint renter` (`Claimant who may be a renter` WITH `regulation 26(2) applies to the claimant` IS TRUE, `claim basis` IS `a single claimant`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 1(2) — a joint renter` (`Claimant who may be a renter` WITH `regulation 26(2) applies to the claimant` IS FALSE, `claim basis` IS `joint claimants`) EQUALS FALSE

-- Schedule 4 paragraph 2, "listed persons": (a) the renter; (b) where the renter is a member of a couple, the other member; (c) a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter (or either joint renter) is responsible.
-- Expected: each limb alone gives TRUE; none gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — a listed person` (`Person who may be a listed person` WITH `the renter` IS TRUE, `the other member of the couple of which the renter is a member` IS FALSE, `a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter (or either joint renter) is responsible` IS FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — a listed person` (`Person who may be a listed person` WITH `the renter` IS FALSE, `the other member of the couple of which the renter is a member` IS TRUE, `a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter (or either joint renter) is responsible` IS FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — a listed person` (`Person who may be a listed person` WITH `the renter` IS FALSE, `the other member of the couple of which the renter is a member` IS FALSE, `a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter (or either joint renter) is responsible` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — a listed person` (`Person who may be a listed person` WITH `the renter` IS FALSE, `the other member of the couple of which the renter is a member` IS FALSE, `a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter (or either joint renter) is responsible` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

GIVEN wales IS A BOOLEAN
      scotland IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord`
`uc3 test — a registered social landlord` wales scotland MEANS
    `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord` WITH
        `registered in the register maintained by the Welsh Ministers under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Housing Act 1996` IS wales
        `registered in the register maintained by the Scottish Housing Regulator under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010` IS scotland

-- Schedule 4 paragraph 2, "registered social landlord": a body registered in the Welsh Ministers' register (a) or the Scottish Housing Regulator's register (b).
-- Expected: either alone gives TRUE; neither gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — registered social landlord` (`uc3 test — a registered social landlord` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — registered social landlord` (`uc3 test — a registered social landlord` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — registered social landlord` (`uc3 test — a registered social landlord` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of council`
      nonProfit IS A BOOLEAN
      profitMaking IS A BOOLEAN
      socialHousing IS A BOOLEAN
      rsl IS A `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord`
GIVETH A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
`uc3 test — a landlord` kind nonProfit profitMaking socialHousing rsl MEANS
    `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing` WITH
        `the landlord as a possible local authority` IS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
            `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS England
            `kind of body` IS kind
        `non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS nonProfit
        `profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS profitMaking
        `the accommodation is social housing` IS socialHousing
        `the landlord as a possible registered social landlord` IS rsl

-- Schedule 4 paragraph 2, "provider of social housing": (a) a local authority; (b) a non-profit registered provider of social housing;
-- (c) in relation to accommodation which is social housing, a profit-making registered provider; (d) a registered social landlord.
-- Expected: each of (a), (b), (d) alone gives TRUE; (c) gives TRUE only when the accommodation is social housing; nothing gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (`uc3 test — a landlord` `a London borough council` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`uc3 test — a registered social landlord` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (`uc3 test — a landlord` `another kind of body` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`uc3 test — a registered social landlord` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (`uc3 test — a landlord` `another kind of body` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`uc3 test — a registered social landlord` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (`uc3 test — a landlord` `another kind of body` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`uc3 test — a registered social landlord` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (`uc3 test — a landlord` `another kind of body` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`uc3 test — a registered social landlord` TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (`uc3 test — a landlord` `another kind of body` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`uc3 test — a registered social landlord` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS FALSE

-- Schedule 4 paragraph 4: no housing costs element for a renter who is 16 or 17 and a care leaver.
-- Expected: 15 gives FALSE; 16 and 17 give TRUE; 18 gives FALSE; 16 and not a care leaver gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 4 — the renter gets no housing costs element as a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` (`Renter who may be a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` WITH `age in complete years` IS 15, `care leaver` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 4 — the renter gets no housing costs element as a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` (`Renter who may be a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` WITH `age in complete years` IS 16, `care leaver` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 4 — the renter gets no housing costs element as a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` (`Renter who may be a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` WITH `age in complete years` IS 17, `care leaver` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 4 — the renter gets no housing costs element as a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` (`Renter who may be a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` WITH `age in complete years` IS 18, `care leaver` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 4 — the renter gets no housing costs element as a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` (`Renter who may be a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` WITH `age in complete years` IS 16, `care leaver` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Schedule 4 paragraph 9: the extended benefit unit.

-- which: 0 none of the exclusions; 1 (a) a person within (1)(a) or (b); 2 (b) the other member of a couple claiming as a single person;
-- 3 (c) a foster child; 4 (d) pays on a commercial basis; 5 (e) the person to whom the liability is owed or their household;
-- 6 (f) already treated as a non-dependant by another claimant; 7 (g) a child or qualifying young person for whom no-one in the unit is responsible.
GIVEN lives IS A BOOLEAN
      which IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Person who may be a non-dependant`
`uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` lives which MEANS
    `Person who may be a non-dependant` WITH
        `normally lives in the accommodation with the renter (or joint renters)` IS lives
        `a person within sub-paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` IS which EQUALS 1
        `where the renter is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple` IS which EQUALS 2
        `the person as a possible foster child` IS `Child who may be a foster child` WITH
            child IS TRUE
            `the child's placement with the renter (or either joint renter)` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
                `nation in which the child is placed` IS England
                `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS which EQUALS 3
                `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS FALSE
        `a person who is liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of the person's occupation of the accommodation` IS which EQUALS 4
        `a person to whom the liability to make relevant payments is owed or a member of their household` IS which EQUALS 5
        `a person who has already been treated as a non-dependant in relation to a claim for universal credit by another person liable to make relevant payments in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter` IS which EQUALS 6
        `a child or qualifying young person for whom no-one in the renter's extended benefit unit is responsible` IS which EQUALS 7

-- Expected: a person who normally lives there and is none of (a) to (g) is a non-dependant (a child who is not fostered is still one);
-- a person who does not live there is not; each of (a) to (g) takes a co-resident out.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` TRUE 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` FALSE 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` TRUE 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` TRUE 2) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` TRUE 3) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` TRUE 4) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` TRUE 5) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` TRUE 6) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(2) — a person is a non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` TRUE 7) EQUALS FALSE

-- Schedule 4 paragraph 9(3): a foster child is a child in relation to whom the renter is a foster parent (regulation 2 "foster parent", England: a child placed under the placement regulations).
-- Expected: a child placed with the renter in England gives TRUE; a child not so placed gives FALSE; a person who is not a child gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(3) — foster child` (`Child who may be a foster child` WITH child IS TRUE, `the child's placement with the renter (or either joint renter)` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH `nation in which the child is placed` IS England, `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS TRUE, `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(3) — foster child` (`Child who may be a foster child` WITH child IS TRUE, `the child's placement with the renter (or either joint renter)` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH `nation in which the child is placed` IS England, `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS FALSE, `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(3) — foster child` (`Child who may be a foster child` WITH child IS FALSE, `the child's placement with the renter (or either joint renter)` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH `nation in which the child is placed` IS England, `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS TRUE, `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

GIVEN renter IS A BOOLEAN
      child IS A BOOLEAN
      nondependant IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may be a member of an extended benefit unit`
`uc3 test — a person who may be in the extended benefit unit` renter child nondependant MEANS
    `Person who may be a member of an extended benefit unit` WITH
        `the renter (or one of joint renters)` IS renter
        `a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible` IS child
        `the person as a possible non-dependant` IS `uc3 test — a person who may live with the renter` nondependant 0

-- Schedule 4 paragraph 9(1): the members are (a) the renter (or joint renters), (b) any child or qualifying young person for whom the renter is responsible, (c) any non-dependant.
-- Expected: each limb alone gives TRUE; a person who lives with the renter and is none of them gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(1) — a person is a member of the renter's extended benefit unit` (`uc3 test — a person who may be in the extended benefit unit` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(1) — a person is a member of the renter's extended benefit unit` (`uc3 test — a person who may be in the extended benefit unit` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(1) — a person is a member of the renter's extended benefit unit` (`uc3 test — a person who may be in the extended benefit unit` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 9(1) — a person is a member of the renter's extended benefit unit` (`uc3 test — a person who may be in the extended benefit unit` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Schedule 4 paragraph 10(1) and (2): the fewest bedrooms for the children.
-- The four kinds are a = boys under 10, b = girls under 10, c = boys 10 or over, d = girls 10 or over (fork U3-F9: sex is two groups).
-- Two children share a bedroom if both are under 10 (para 10(1)(d)) or both are of the same sex (10(1)(e)); any other child has one (10(1)(f));
-- a child to whom two descriptions apply goes to the one that gives the fewest bedrooms (10(2)).
-- Expected (counted by hand from those two sharing rules):
--   no children 0;  one boy under 10  1;  two boys under 10  1 (both limbs);  a boy and a girl under 10  1 (limb (d));
--   a boy and a girl both 10 or over  2 (neither limb);  two boys 10 or over  1 (limb (e));  a boy under 10 and a girl 10 or over  2 (neither limb);
--   one of each of the four kinds  2 (boy with boy, girl with girl: limb (e) twice; pairing by age instead would give 3);
--   one boy 10 or over and three girls under 10  3 (two girls share, the third girl and the boy are alone);
--   five children, 2 + 2 + 1 boys 10 or over  3;  three children under 10 (one boy, two girls)  2;  six boys, three under 10 and three 10 or over  3;
--   one girl under 10 and two girls 10 or over  2.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 1 0 0 0 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 2 0 0 0 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 1 1 0 0 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 0 0 1 1 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 0 0 2 0 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 1 0 0 1 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 1 1 1 1 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 0 3 1 0 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 2 2 1 0 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 1 2 0 0 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 3 0 3 0 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for children of four kinds` 0 1 0 2 EQUALS 2

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit`
`uc3 test — children` a b c d MEANS
    `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit` WITH
        `male children under 10 years old` IS a
        `female children under 10 years old` IS b
        `male children aged 10 or over` IS c
        `female children aged 10 or over` IS d

-- The record form of the same rule, and the number of children.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(2) — the fewest bedrooms for a group of children` (`uc3 test — children` 1 1 1 1) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10(1)(d) to (f) — the number of children in a group` (`uc3 test — children` 1 2 3 4) EQUALS 10

-- Paragraph 12(8): the children who are left when the disabled ones are taken out, kind by kind and never below nil.
-- Expected: 2 boys under 10 less 1 boy under 10 leaves 1; 1 girl 10 or over less 3 girls 10 or over leaves 0 (never below nil).
#ASSERT (`Sch 4 para 12(8) — the children who are left when the children with the disabled child condition are taken out` (`uc3 test — children` 2 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0))'s `male children under 10 years old` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`Sch 4 para 12(8) — the children who are left when the children with the disabled child condition are taken out` (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 1) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 3))'s `female children aged 10 or over` EQUALS 0

-- A person who satisfies the overnight care condition (para 12(3)): in receipt of one of the seven payments (here payment 6, the daily living component of
-- personal independence payment), with carers who live elsewhere and stay overnight regularly, under arrangements made for that purpose.
GIVEN payments IS A `Disability payments of a person`
      carers IS A BOOLEAN
      arrangements IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may satisfy the overnight care condition`
`uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` payments carers arrangements MEANS
    `Person who may satisfy the overnight care condition` WITH
        payments IS payments
        `one or more persons who do not live in the renter's accommodation are engaged to provide overnight care for the person and to stay overnight in the accommodation on a regular basis` IS carers
        `overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose` IS arrangements

-- Paragraph 12(3): all three of (a) receipt, (b) carers who stay overnight, (c) arrangements for that purpose.
-- Expected: all three gives TRUE; receipt missing, or only entitlement without receipt, or carers missing, or arrangements missing, gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(3) — a person satisfies the overnight care condition` (`uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6) TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(3) — a person satisfies the overnight care condition` (`uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` `uc3 test — no disability payment` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(3) — a person satisfies the overnight care condition` (`uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is entitled to but not received` 6) TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(3) — a person satisfies the overnight care condition` (`uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6) FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(3) — a person satisfies the overnight care condition` (`uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(3) — a person satisfies the overnight care condition` (`uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 5) TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(A1) — one or more of the persons listed satisfies the overnight care condition` (LIST `uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` `uc3 test — no disability payment` TRUE TRUE, `uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 4) TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(A1) — one or more of the persons listed satisfies the overnight care condition` (LIST `uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` `uc3 test — no disability payment` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(A1) — one or more of the persons listed satisfies the overnight care condition` EMPTY EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Schedule 4 paragraph 11: temporary absence. Dates are written with YMD. The first six months of an absence that begins on 1 January 2025 run to 30 June 2025
-- and the next day is outside them (fork U3-F8 in NOTES.md: the text does not say how a month is counted from a day, and the expectations here follow the reading taken there).

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      first IS A DATE
      which IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Temporarily absent child or qualifying young person`
`uc3 test — an absent child` day first which MEANS
    `Temporarily absent child or qualifying young person` WITH
        `day to which the determination relates` IS day
        `first day of the absence` IS first
        `the renter is treated as not being responsible for the child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(6)(a)` IS (which EQUALS 1) OR (which EQUALS 5)
        `immediately before the local authority started looking after them the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element` IS which EQUALS 1
        `the renter is treated as not being responsible for the child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(6)(b)` IS (which EQUALS 2) OR (which EQUALS 4) OR (which EQUALS 6)
        `immediately before becoming a prisoner the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element` IS (which EQUALS 2) OR (which EQUALS 4)
        `the child or qualifying young person has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months` IS which EQUALS 2
        `the determination relates to a time before the renter or joint renter ceases to be responsible for the temporarily absent child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(7)` IS which EQUALS 3

-- which: 1 looked after by a local authority and included before; 2 a prisoner, included before, not sentenced beyond the 6 months; 3 before responsibility ceases (reg 4(7));
-- 4 a prisoner, included before, but sentenced beyond the 6 months; 5 looked after but not included before; 6 a prisoner who was not included before.
-- Para 11(2)(a): the determination relates to any time during the first 6 months of the absence, where the child was in the unit and the award included the housing costs element just before.
-- Expected: 30 June 2025 is inside (TRUE); 1 July 2025 is outside (FALSE); a day before the absence began is outside (FALSE); if the child was not included just before, FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2)(a) — looked after by a local authority` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2)(a) — looked after by a local authority` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2)(a) — looked after by a local authority` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2)(a) — looked after by a local authority` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 5) EQUALS FALSE
-- Para 11(2)(b): a prisoner, included before, and not sentenced to a term expected to extend beyond that 6 months.
-- Expected: 30 June 2025 gives TRUE; 1 July 2025 gives FALSE; sentenced beyond the 6 months gives FALSE; not included before gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2)(b) — a prisoner` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 2) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2)(b) — a prisoner` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 2) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2)(b) — a prisoner` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 4) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2)(b) — a prisoner` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 6) EQUALS FALSE
-- Para 11(2)(c): any time before responsibility ceases under reg 4(7): the dates do not matter.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2)(c) — before responsibility ceases under regulation 4(7)` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2031 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 3) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2)(c) — before responsibility ceases under regulation 4(7)` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Para 11(2) as a whole: any one of (a), (b), (c) includes the child.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2) — a temporarily absent child or qualifying young person is included` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2) — a temporarily absent child or qualifying young person is included` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 2) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2) — a temporarily absent child or qualifying young person is included` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2031 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 3) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(2) — a temporarily absent child or qualifying young person is included` (`uc3 test — an absent child` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1) EQUALS FALSE

-- Para 11(3): a temporarily absent renter is included when the absence from Great Britain is disregarded (reg 11(1) or (2)), or the renter is a prisoner to whom reg 19(2) applies.
-- Expected: either alone gives TRUE; neither gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(3) — a temporarily absent renter is included` (`Temporarily absent renter` WITH `the temporary absence from Great Britain of the renter is disregarded in accordance with regulation 11(1) or (2)` IS TRUE, `the renter is a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies` IS FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(3) — a temporarily absent renter is included` (`Temporarily absent renter` WITH `the temporary absence from Great Britain of the renter is disregarded in accordance with regulation 11(1) or (2)` IS FALSE, `the renter is a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(3) — a temporarily absent renter is included` (`Temporarily absent renter` WITH `the temporary absence from Great Britain of the renter is disregarded in accordance with regulation 11(1) or (2)` IS FALSE, `the renter is a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- A non-dependant who is temporarily absent. which: 1 abroad (first month); 2 abroad, the circumstances of a death of a close relative (reg 11(2)); 3 abroad for treatment (reg 11(3)(a));
-- 4 a prisoner not sentenced beyond the 6 months; 5 a prisoner sentenced beyond it; 6 a son or daughter in the armed forces away on operations;
-- 7 a member of the armed forces away on operations who is not a son or daughter.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      first IS A DATE
      which IS A NUMBER
      inUnit IS A BOOLEAN
      award IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Temporarily absent non-dependant`
`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` day first which inUnit award MEANS
    `Temporarily absent non-dependant` WITH
        `day to which the determination relates` IS day
        `first day of the absence` IS first
        `the absence is a temporary absence from Great Britain` IS (which EQUALS 1) OR (which EQUALS 2) OR (which EQUALS 3)
        `the circumstances of the non-dependant are such as would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2)` IS which EQUALS 2
        `the absence from Great Britain is in the circumstances described in regulation 11(3)(a)` IS which EQUALS 3
        `the non-dependant is a prisoner` IS (which EQUALS 4) OR (which EQUALS 5)
        `the non-dependant has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months` IS which EQUALS 4
        `the non-dependant is the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters` IS which EQUALS 6
        `the non-dependant is a member of the armed forces away on operations` IS (which EQUALS 6) OR (which EQUALS 7)
        `immediately before the start of the period the non-dependant was included in the renter's extended benefit unit` IS inUnit
        `immediately before the start of the period the renter's award included the housing costs element` IS award

-- Para 11(5)(a): the first month of the absence from Great Britain, and a further month if the circumstances are those of reg 11(2) (death of a close relative).
-- Expected: absence from 1 January 2025: 31 January is inside the first month (TRUE), 1 February is outside (FALSE);
-- with the reg 11(2) circumstances: 28 February is inside the further month (TRUE) and 1 March is outside (FALSE); without them 28 February is outside (FALSE).
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(a) — the first month of an absence from Great Britain, and a further month` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(a) — the first month of an absence from Great Britain, and a further month` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(a) — the first month of an absence from Great Britain, and a further month` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 2 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(a) — the first month of an absence from Great Britain, and a further month` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 2 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(a) — the first month of an absence from Great Britain, and a further month` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Para 11(5)(b): the first 6 months of an absence from Great Britain solely for treatment. Expected: 30 June TRUE, 1 July FALSE; an absence not for treatment FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(b) — the first 6 months of an absence for treatment` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 3 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(b) — the first 6 months of an absence for treatment` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 3 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(b) — the first 6 months of an absence for treatment` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Para 11(5)(c): the first 6 months as a prisoner not sentenced beyond that period. Expected: 30 June TRUE, 1 July FALSE, sentenced beyond FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(c) — the first 6 months as a prisoner` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 4 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(c) — the first 6 months as a prisoner` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 4 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(c) — the first 6 months as a prisoner` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 5 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Para 11(5)(d): any period in which a son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter is in the armed forces away on operations: the dates do not matter; another relative does not qualify.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(d) — a son or daughter in the armed forces away on operations` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2031 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 6 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(5)(d) — a son or daughter in the armed forces away on operations` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2031 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 7 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Para 11(4): the non-dependant was in the unit just before the period and, for periods (a) to (c), the award included the housing costs element; for (d) only the first.
-- Expected: (a) with both TRUE; (a) with the award missing FALSE; (a) with not in the unit FALSE; (d) with the award missing TRUE; (d) with not in the unit FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(4) — a temporarily absent non-dependant is included` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(4) — a temporarily absent non-dependant is included` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(4) — a temporarily absent non-dependant is included` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(4) — a temporarily absent non-dependant is included` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 1 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(4) — a temporarily absent non-dependant is included` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2031 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 6 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(4) — a temporarily absent non-dependant is included` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2031 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 6 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(4) — a temporarily absent non-dependant is included` (`uc3 test — an absent non-dependant` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 4 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- Para 11(6): a non-dependant absent in other circumstances is not treated as a member of the unit if the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 6 months.
-- Expected (fork U3-F8, an absence from 1 January 2025 has lasted exactly 6 months at 30 June and exceeds them from 1 July):
-- a determination on 1 July 2025 gives TRUE (not a member); on 30 June 2025 with the absence expected to last to 30 June gives FALSE;
-- on 30 June 2025 with the absence expected to last to 1 July 2025 gives TRUE; in the circumstances of (4) and (5) it gives FALSE.
GIVEN other IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
      expectedEnd IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Non-dependant absent in other circumstances`
`uc3 test — a non-dependant absent in other circumstances` other day expectedEnd MEANS
    `Non-dependant absent in other circumstances` WITH
        `the absence is in circumstances other than those specified in sub-paragraphs (4) and (5)` IS other
        `first day of the absence` IS YearMonthDay 2025 1 1
        `day to which the determination relates` IS day
        `last day to which the absence is expected to last` IS expectedEnd

#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(6) — an absent non-dependant is not treated as a member of the extended benefit unit` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant absent in other circumstances` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(6) — an absent non-dependant is not treated as a member of the extended benefit unit` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant absent in other circumstances` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(6) — an absent non-dependant is not treated as a member of the extended benefit unit` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant absent in other circumstances` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 11(6) — an absent non-dependant is not treated as a member of the extended benefit unit` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant absent in other circumstances` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)) EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Schedule 4 paragraph 12: the additional bedroom.

-- A renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition. placed: a child is placed with the renter in England under the placement regulations; wouldBe: would be a foster parent
-- but for having no child placed now; adopter: an adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption; lastEnded: the day the last placement ended; day: the day asked about.
GIVEN placed IS A BOOLEAN
      wouldBe IS A BOOLEAN
      adopter IS A BOOLEAN
      lastEnded IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition`
`uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` placed wouldBe adopter lastEnded day MEANS
    `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition` WITH
        `the renter's placement of a child` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
            `nation in which the child is placed` IS England
            `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS placed
            `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS FALSE
        `the renter would be a foster parent but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them` IS wouldBe
        `the day the renter's last placement ended or, if no child has yet been placed with them, the day on which they were approved to be a foster parent` IS lastEnded
        `day to which the determination relates` IS day
        `adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption` IS adopter

-- Para 12(4) and (5): a foster parent, an adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption, or a person who would be a foster parent but for having no child placed now,
-- if the period since the last placement ended (or since approval) does not exceed 12 months.
-- Expected: a child placed gives TRUE; an adopter gives TRUE; a would-be foster parent whose last placement ended on 1 January 2025 satisfies it on 31 December 2025 (12 months not exceeded, TRUE)
-- and not on 1 January 2026 (exceeded, FALSE; fork U3-F8); a would-be foster parent with no placement and no such status gives FALSE; no fact at all gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(4) — a renter satisfies the foster parent condition` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(4) — a renter satisfies the foster parent condition` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(4) — a renter satisfies the foster parent condition` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` FALSE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(4) — a renter satisfies the foster parent condition` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` FALSE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(4) — a renter satisfies the foster parent condition` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(5) — a person who would be a foster parent but for having no child placed` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` FALSE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31)) EQUALS TRUE

GIVEN payments IS A `Disability payments of a person`
      cannotShare IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Child who may satisfy the disabled child condition`
`uc3 test — a child who may be disabled` payments cannotShare MEANS
    `Child who may satisfy the disabled child condition` WITH
        payments IS payments
        `by virtue of their disability, the child is not reasonably able to share a room with another child` IS cannotShare

-- Para 12(6)(a) and (b): in receipt of the care component of disability living allowance (payment 1) or of child disability payment (payment 2) at the middle or highest rate,
-- and by virtue of disability not reasonably able to share a room with another child.
-- Expected: payment 1 or 2 with the inability gives TRUE; payment 1 without the inability FALSE; payment 4 (attendance allowance) with the inability FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) and (b) — a child in receipt of a listed care component who cannot share a room` (`uc3 test — a child who may be disabled` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 1) TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) and (b) — a child in receipt of a listed care component who cannot share a room` (`uc3 test — a child who may be disabled` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 2) TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) and (b) — a child in receipt of a listed care component who cannot share a room` (`uc3 test — a child who may be disabled` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 1) FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) and (b) — a child in receipt of a listed care component who cannot share a room` (`uc3 test — a child who may be disabled` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 4) TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

GIVEN expectedToShare IS A BOOLEAN
      payments IS A `Disability payments of a person`
      cannotShare IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Renter who may satisfy the disabled person condition`
`uc3 test — a renter who may be disabled` expectedToShare payments cannotShare MEANS
    `Renter who may satisfy the disabled person condition` WITH
        `the renter would, but for the provisions of this paragraph, be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter` IS expectedToShare
        payments IS payments
        `by virtue of their disability, the renter is not reasonably able to share a bedroom with the joint renter` IS cannotShare

-- Para 12(6A): a renter who would be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter, in receipt of one of the seven payments (here the care component of child disability payment, payment 2,
-- which the seven include and the child condition also includes, and the daily living component of adult disability payment, payment 7), and by virtue of disability unable to share.
-- Expected: all three gives TRUE; not expected to share FALSE; no payment FALSE; able to share FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6A) — a renter satisfies the disabled person condition` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be disabled` TRUE (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7) TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6A) — a renter satisfies the disabled person condition` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be disabled` TRUE (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 2) TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6A) — a renter satisfies the disabled person condition` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be disabled` FALSE (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7) TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6A) — a renter satisfies the disabled person condition` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be disabled` TRUE `uc3 test — no disability payment` TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6A) — a renter satisfies the disabled person condition` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be disabled` TRUE (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7) FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A whole extended benefit unit, and the number of bedrooms. The renter (or joint renters together) always count one bedroom (para 10(1)(a)).

GIVEN qyp IS A NUMBER
      nondependants IS A NUMBER
      children IS A `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit`
      disabledChildren IS A `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit`
      overnight IS A LIST OF `Person who may satisfy the overnight care condition`
      foster IS A LIST OF `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition`
      disabledPersons IS A LIST OF `Renter who may satisfy the disabled person condition`
GIVETH A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
`uc3 test — a unit` qyp nondependants children disabledChildren overnight foster disabledPersons MEANS
    `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria` WITH
        `qualifying young persons for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible` IS qyp
        `non-dependants who are not children` IS nondependants
        children IS children
        `disabled children` IS disabledChildren
        `persons who may satisfy the overnight care condition` IS overnight
        `renters as holders of the foster parent condition` IS foster
        `renters as holders of the disabled person condition` IS disabledPersons

GIVEN qyp IS A NUMBER
      nondependants IS A NUMBER
      a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria`
`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` qyp nondependants a b c d MEANS
    `uc3 test — a unit` qyp nondependants (`uc3 test — children` a b c d) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY

-- Para 10(1): one bedroom for the renter (or joint renters), one for each qualifying young person, one for each non-dependant who is not a child, and the fewest for the children.
-- Expected (counted from the sub-paragraphs): renter alone 1; renter and a qualifying young person 2; renter and two non-dependants 3;
-- renter and a boy and a girl under 10  2 (the children share); renter and a boy and a girl both 10 or over  3 (they do not);
-- renter, 1 qualifying young person, 2 non-dependants and two boys under 10  1 + 1 + 2 + 1 = 5.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` 0 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` 1 0 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` 0 2 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` 0 0 1 1 0 0) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` 0 0 0 0 1 1) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` 1 2 2 0 0 0) EQUALS 5

-- Para 26 (Part 4 only): no renter is entitled to more than 4 bedrooms. Expected: 4 stays 4; 5 becomes 4; 3 stays 3. Para 10 alone (Part 5) is not capped: 5 stays 5.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 26 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled under Part 4` (`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` 1 2 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 26 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled under Part 4` (`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` 1 2 2 0 0 0) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 26 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled under Part 4` (`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` 1 1 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit with no additional bedroom` 3 1 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 5

-- Para 12(A1) and (9)(a): one additional bedroom if one or more persons satisfy the overnight care condition (one, not one for each person).
-- Expected: renter alone with one person who satisfies it  2;  with two such persons  2;  with a person who does not (no payment)  1.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6) TRUE TRUE) EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6) TRUE TRUE, `uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 4) TRUE TRUE) EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` `uc3 test — no disability payment` TRUE TRUE) EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 1

-- Para 12(1)(b) and (9)(b): one additional bedroom if the renter, or one or both of joint renters, satisfies the foster parent condition.
-- Expected: one foster parent 2; joint renters who both satisfy it 2 (one additional bedroom, not two); neither 1.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) EMPTY (LIST `uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)) EMPTY) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) EMPTY (LIST `uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1), `uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)) EMPTY) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) EMPTY (LIST `uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)) EMPTY) EQUALS 1

-- Para 12(1)(d), (6A) and (9)(d): one additional bedroom if the renter, or one or both of joint renters, satisfies the disabled person condition.
-- Expected: one joint renter who satisfies it 2; neither 1.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `uc3 test — a renter who may be disabled` TRUE (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7) TRUE)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 0 0) EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `uc3 test — a renter who may be disabled` TRUE `uc3 test — no disability payment` TRUE)) EQUALS 1

-- Para 12(8): as many additional bedrooms as are necessary to ensure that each child with the disabled child condition has their own bedroom (fork U3-F11).
-- Expected, counted by hand:
--   two boys under 10, one of them disabled:  they would share one bedroom; each now has one, so 1 more:  renter 1 + children 1 + 1 = 3;
--   one boy under 10, disabled, alone:  already alone, so no more:  1 + 1 + 0 = 2;
--   a disabled boy 10 or over and a girl 10 or over:  they already do not share:  1 + 2 + 0 = 3;
--   a disabled boy under 10, a boy 10 or over and a girl 10 or over:  the disabled boy shares with the other boy by sex, so 1 more:  1 + 2 + 1 = 4;
--   two disabled boys under 10:  each needs their own, which is 1 more than the shared one:  1 + 1 + 1 = 3.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 2 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 1 1) (`uc3 test — children` 0 0 1 0) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 1 1) (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 2 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 2 0 0 0) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(8) — the additional bedrooms for the disabled child condition` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 2 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6) — the renter satisfies the disabled child condition` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 2 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 12(6) — the renter satisfies the disabled child condition` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS FALSE

-- All four additional bedrooms together (para 12(9)): renter 1, children (two boys under 10, one disabled) 1, and 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 additional = 6; capped at 4 in Part 4 (para 26).
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 2 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6) TRUE TRUE) (LIST `uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)) (LIST `uc3 test — a renter who may be disabled` TRUE (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7) TRUE)) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 26 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled under Part 4` (`uc3 test — a unit` 0 0 (`uc3 test — children` 2 0 0 0) (`uc3 test — children` 1 0 0 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a person who may need overnight care` (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 6) TRUE TRUE) (LIST `uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)) (LIST `uc3 test — a renter who may be disabled` TRUE (`uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7) TRUE)) EQUALS 4

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Schedule 4 paragraph 29(10): "hostel" and "hostel for homeless people".

-- A building. accommodation: domestic accommodation for persons generally, not separate and self-contained; board; food: facilities for food preparation;
-- owner: 0 no social housing provider, 1 a non-profit registered provider (not a local authority), 2 a local authority (a London borough council);
-- funded: 0 neither; 1 operated other than on a commercial basis and funded in whole or part by a government department, agency or local authority; 2 funded but run on a commercial basis; 3 run non-commercially but not funded;
-- voluntary: managed by a voluntary organisation; supervision: provides care, support or supervision with a view to rehabilitation or resettlement; careHome: England care home.
GIVEN accommodation IS A BOOLEAN
      board IS A BOOLEAN
      food IS A BOOLEAN
      owner IS A NUMBER
      funded IS A NUMBER
      voluntary IS A BOOLEAN
      supervision IS A BOOLEAN
      careHome IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Building that may be a hostel`
`uc3 test — a building` accommodation board food owner funded voluntary supervision careHome MEANS
    `Building that may be a hostel` WITH
        `domestic accommodation is provided for persons generally or for a class of persons otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises` IS accommodation
        `board is provided` IS board
        `facilities for the preparation of food adequate to the needs of those persons are provided` IS food
        `the owner or manager as a possible provider of social housing` IS `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing` WITH
            `the landlord as a possible local authority` IS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
                `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS England
                `kind of body` IS IF owner EQUALS 2 THEN `a London borough council` ELSE `another kind of body`
            `non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS owner EQUALS 1
            `profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS FALSE
            `the accommodation is social housing` IS FALSE
            `the landlord as a possible registered social landlord` IS `uc3 test — a registered social landlord` FALSE FALSE
        `the building is operated other than on a commercial basis` IS (funded EQUALS 1) OR (funded EQUALS 3)
        `funds are provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority` IS (funded EQUALS 1) OR (funded EQUALS 2)
        `the manager as a possible voluntary organisation` IS `uc3 test — a body` `another kind of body` FALSE voluntary
        `the manager as a possible registered charity` IS `Charity that may be a registered charity` WITH `entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE, `entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` IS FALSE
        `the building provides care, support or supervision with a view to assisting those persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS supervision
        `the building as possible care home premises` IS `uc3 test — premises` England careHome FALSE FALSE (`uc3 test — a hospital` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- "hostel": a building (a) with domestic accommodation not in separate and self-contained premises, and either board or facilities for preparing food or both; and
-- (b) which is (i) managed or owned by a provider of social housing other than a local authority, or (ii) operated other than on a commercial basis and funded in whole or part by
-- a government department or agency or a local authority, or (iii) managed by a voluntary organisation or a registered charity and providing care, support or supervision; and (c) is not a care home.
-- Expected: accommodation and board and a non-profit provider  TRUE;  accommodation and food only and funded (ii)  TRUE;
-- the same but owned by a local authority only  FALSE (limb (i) excludes a local authority);  no board and no food  FALSE;  no domestic accommodation  FALSE;
-- accommodation and board but only a voluntary manager without care (iii)  FALSE;  with care  TRUE;  a care home that otherwise meets (a) and (b)  FALSE (limb (c)).
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel` (`uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel` (`uc3 test — a building` TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel` (`uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 2 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel` (`uc3 test — a building` TRUE FALSE FALSE 1 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel` (`uc3 test — a building` FALSE TRUE TRUE 1 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel` (`uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel` (`uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel` (`uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Limb (b)(ii) needs both halves: operated other than on a commercial basis AND funded. Expected: funded but run commercially FALSE; run non-commercially but not funded FALSE; both TRUE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)(ii)` (`uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)(ii)` (`uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel, limb (b)(ii)` (`uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE

-- "hostel for homeless people": a hostel the main purpose of which is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to rehabilitation or resettlement.
-- Expected: a hostel with that main purpose TRUE; a hostel without it FALSE; that purpose in a building that is not a hostel (no board or food) FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel for homeless people` (`Building that may be a hostel for homeless people` WITH `the building as a possible hostel` IS `uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE, `the main purpose of the building is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to assisting such persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel for homeless people` (`Building that may be a hostel for homeless people` WITH `the building as a possible hostel` IS `uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE, `the main purpose of the building is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to assisting such persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — hostel for homeless people` (`Building that may be a hostel for homeless people` WITH `the building as a possible hostel` IS `uc3 test — a building` TRUE FALSE FALSE 1 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE, `the main purpose of the building is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to assisting such persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- "person acting in an official capacity": a health care professional, a police officer, a registered social worker, the victim's employer, or a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence.
-- Expected: each of the five alone gives TRUE; none gives FALSE.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Person who may be a person acting in an official capacity`
`uc3 test — a person who may be acting in an official capacity` n MEANS
    `Person who may be a person acting in an official capacity` WITH
        `health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)` IS n EQUALS 1
        `police officer` IS n EQUALS 2
        `registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)` IS n EQUALS 3
        `the victim's employer` IS n EQUALS 4
        `a public, voluntary, or charitable body which has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence` IS n EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — person acting in an official capacity` (`uc3 test — a person who may be acting in an official capacity` 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — person acting in an official capacity` (`uc3 test — a person who may be acting in an official capacity` 2) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — person acting in an official capacity` (`uc3 test — a person who may be acting in an official capacity` 3) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — person acting in an official capacity` (`uc3 test — a person who may be acting in an official capacity` 4) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — person acting in an official capacity` (`uc3 test — a person who may be acting in an official capacity` 5) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 29(10) — person acting in an official capacity` (`uc3 test — a person who may be acting in an official capacity` 0) EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Schedule 4 paragraph 29: the excepted person, E.

GIVEN months IS A NUMBER
      mainPurpose IS A BOOLEAN
      services IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Stay in a hostel`
`uc3 test — a stay in a hostel` months mainPurpose services MEANS
    `Stay in a hostel` WITH
        `the hostel` IS `Building that may be a hostel for homeless people` WITH
            `the building as a possible hostel` IS `uc3 test — a building` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE
            `the main purpose of the building is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to assisting such persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS mainPurpose
        `months the stay lasted` IS months
        `whilst living in the hostel E was offered and has accepted services which the Secretary of State considers are intended to assist E to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS services

-- limb: 0 none of the limbs; 2 a care leaver (para 29(2)); 4 stays totalling 3 months in hostels for homeless people, with services accepted (29(4));
-- 5 in receipt of a listed payment (29(5), payment 7 here); 6 active multi-agency management (29(6)); 7 active multi-agency risk management (29(7));
-- 8 section 10(1)(b) or (d) not in force and serious harm (29(8)); 9 section 10(1)(e) not in force and serious harm by reason of an offence (29(9));
-- 91 foster parent (29(9A)); 92 domestic violence with evidence from two persons in an official capacity (29(9B)); 93 positive conclusive grounds determination (29(9C)).
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
      nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      limb IS A NUMBER
      stays IS A LIST OF `Stay in a hostel`
GIVETH A `Renter who may be an excepted person`
`uc3 test — a renter who may be an excepted person` age nation limb stays MEANS
    `Renter who may be an excepted person` WITH
        `age in complete years` IS age
        `nation of Great Britain to which the renter is related` IS nation
        `was a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18` IS limb EQUALS 2
        `stays in hostels` IS stays
        payments IS IF limb EQUALS 5 THEN `uc3 test — only payment n is received` 7 ELSE `uc3 test — no disability payment`
        `active multi-agency management pursuant to arrangements established by a responsible authority under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003` IS limb EQUALS 6
        `active multi-agency risk management pursuant to arrangements established by the responsible authorities under section 10(1) of the 2005 Act` IS limb EQUALS 7
        `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(b) or (d) has not been brought fully into force` IS limb EQUALS 8
        `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(e) has not been brought fully into force` IS limb EQUALS 9
        `considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large` IS limb EQUALS 8
        `by reason of an offence of which they have been convicted, considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large` IS limb EQUALS 9
        `the renter as a possible holder of the foster parent condition` IS `uc3 test — a renter who may be a foster parent` (limb EQUALS 91) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1)
        `after attaining the age of 16 had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them by their partner or former partner, or by a relative` IS limb EQUALS 92
        `the person who provides evidence that the circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened` IS `uc3 test — a person who may be acting in an official capacity` (IF limb EQUALS 92 THEN 2 ELSE 0)
        `the victim's circumstances are consistent with their having had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them` IS limb EQUALS 92
        `the person whom the victim has contacted in relation to such an incident` IS `uc3 test — a person who may be acting in an official capacity` (IF limb EQUALS 92 THEN 3 ELSE 0)
        `a competent authority has determined that the renter is a victim of trafficking in human beings, slavery, servitude or forced or compulsory labour` IS limb EQUALS 93

